Subject: Recharged title logo
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The port is called Recharged (issue #64), and its logo says so (issue #63):
wherever the game draws its logo, on the title screen, in the main menu and
on Domination's captain select, the word under STRIKERS reads RECHARGED, on
every release of the game.

FEScene::LoadPackage hands each front-end scene file, as read from the disc,
to the port (src/platform/recharged_logo_hook.cpp). A scene that draws the
logo comes back rewritten: copies of the game's own animated R and E letters
in front of its "charged" letters, the longer word drawn at 90 % so that it
fits the logo's black backdrop, and the lightning around it extended to the
new letters. Every
other scene is left as it is. Like the listed bug fixes the change is always
on, outside the tweak mask; the host's RECHARGED_ORIGINAL_LOGO=1 keeps the
original logo. The hook exists only in the native game module.

diff --git a/src/Game/FE/feScene.cpp b/src/Game/FE/feScene.cpp
index 2a5eaf7..c6a046f 100644
--- a/src/Game/FE/feScene.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/FE/feScene.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
 #include "platform/frontend_package.h"
 #endif
+#include "mscharged_tweaks.h"
 
 struct FE_FILE_HEADER
 {
@@ -154,6 +155,12 @@ inline void FEScene::LoadPackageResources(FEPackage* pFEPackage)
 
 void FEScene::LoadPackage(void* pData, unsigned long uSize)
 {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port (issue #63): the logo of the title screen, the main menu and the
+    // captain select reads RECHARGED. A scene that draws it comes back
+    // rewritten: R and E in front of its "charged" letters.
+    pData = mscharged_tweak_frontend_package(pData, &uSize);
+#endif
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
     auto nativePackage = mscharged::platform::PrepareFrontendPackage(pData, uSize);
     pData = nativePackage.Data();
